ll business operator is an association of employees that is registered or recognised under the Fair Work (Registered Organisations) Act 2009, this Act applies, with the prescribed modifications (if any), in relation to the activities carried on by the small business operator, as if the small business operator were an organisation (within the meaning of this Act). Note: The regulations may prescribe different modifications of the Act for different small business operators. See subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Small business operator that is accredited for the consumer data right regime  (1D) If a small business operator holds an accreditation under subsection 56CA(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010, this Act applies, with the prescribed modifications (if any), in relation to information that:  (a) is personal information; but  (b) is not CDR data (within the meaning of that Act); as if the small business operator were an organisation. Note: The regulations may prescribe different modifications of the Act for different small business operators. See subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Regulations treating a small business operator as an organisation  (1) This Act applies, with the prescribed modifications (if any), in relation to a small business operator prescribed for the purposes of this subsection as if the small business operator were an organisation. Note 1: The regulations may prescribe different modifications of the Act for different small business operators. See subsection 33(3A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer .

