doc:sch-2-sec-6j a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "6J Securitisation arrangements etc." ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) an organisation or small business operator (the securitisation entity) carries on a business that is involved in either or both of the following:  (i) a securitisation arrangement;  (ii) managing credit that is the subject of a securitisation arrangement; and  (b) the securitisation entity performs a task that is reasonably necessary for:  (i) purchasing, funding or managing, or processing an application for, credit by means of a securitisation arrangement; or  (ii) undertaking credit enhancement in relation to credit; and  (c) the credit has been provided by, or is credit for which an application has been made to, a credit provider (the original credit provider);" ;
    cof:pageNumber "71"^^xsd:integer .

concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-6k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6K Acquisition of the rights of a credit provider"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-6k ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) an organisation or small business operator (the acquirer) acquires, whether by assignment, subrogation or any other means, the rights of a credit provider (the original credit provider) in relation to the repayment of an amount of credit; and  (b) the acquirer is not a credit provider under subsection 6G(1); then the acquirer is a credit provider but only in relation to the credit.  (2) If subsection (1) of this section applies in relation to credit that has been provided by the original credit provider, the credit is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been provided by the acquirer.  (3) If subsection (1) of this section applies in relation to credit for which an application has been made to the original credit provider, the application is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been made to the acquirer.   Interpretation  Part II Key definitions relating to credit reporting  Division 2  Section 6L  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Subdivision B—Other definitions" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) an organisation or small business operator (the acquirer) acquires, whether by assignment, subrogation or any other means, the rights of a credit provider (the original credit provider) in relation to the repayment of an amount of credit; and  (b) the acquirer is not a credit provider under subsection 6G(1); then the acquirer is a credit provider but only in relation to the credit.  (2) If subsection (1) of this section applies in relation to credit that has been provided by the original credit provider, the credit is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been provided by the acquirer.  (3) If subsection (1) of this section applies in relation to credit for which an application has been made to the original credit provider, the application is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to have been made to the acquirer.   Interpretation  Part II Key definitions relating to credit reporting  Division 2  Section 6L  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Subdivision B—Other definitions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "640905ea00716a0b0cb3383c2d4a085015d65372f45e3b46e6eeb633535b591a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "72"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-6k-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-6k-ss-2 ;
