    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-6q-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Default information about an individual is information about a payment that the individual is overdue in making as a guarantor under a guarantee given against any default by a person (the borrower) in repaying all or any of the debt deferred under consumer credit provided by a credit provider to the borrower if:  (a) the provider has given the individual written notice of the borrower’s default that gave rise to the individual’s obligation to make the overdue payment; and  (b) the notice requests that the individual pay the amount of the overdue payment; and  (c) at least 60 days have passed since the day on which the notice was given; and   Interpretation  Part II Key definitions relating to credit reporting  Division 2  Section 6QA  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (d) in addition to giving the notice, the provider has taken other steps to recover the amount of the overdue payment from the individual; and  (e) the provider is not prevented by a statute of limitations from recovering the amount of the overdue payment." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Default information about an individual is information about a payment that the individual is overdue in making as a guarantor under a guarantee given against any default by a person (the borrower) in repaying all or any of the debt deferred under consumer credit provided by a credit provider to the borrower if:  (a) the provider has given the individual written notice of the borrower’s default that gave rise to the individual’s obligation to make the overdue payment; and  (b) the notice requests that the individual pay the amount of the overdue payment; and  (c) at least 60 days have passed since the day on which the notice was given; and   Interpretation  Part II Key definitions relating to credit reporting  Division 2  Section 6QA  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (d) in addition to giving the notice, the provider has taken other steps to recover the amount of the overdue payment from the individual; and  (e) the provider is not prevented by a statute of limitations from recovering the amount of the overdue payment."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8efe51387a938af9853af68c3e4ecb5e96b529be5f2b0d290d5c0d71b9f24498" ;
    values:partOf concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-6q ;
