    skos:definition "(1) An entity contravenes this subsection if:  (a) the entity does an act, or engages in a practice, that is an interference with the privacy of an individual; and  (b) the interference with privacy is serious.   Information privacy  Part III Interferences with privacy  Division 1  Section 13G  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Note: The court may determine that an entity has contravened section 13H if the court is satisfied of paragraph (a) but not paragraph (b) (see section 13J)."@en ;
