    values:originalText "If, in proceedings for an order in relation to a contravention of section 13G, the court:  (a) is satisfied that the entity has done an act, or engaged in a practice, that is an interference with the privacy of an individual; but  (b) is not satisfied that the interference with privacy is serious; the court may make a pecuniary penalty order against the entity for contravening section 13H, instead of section 13G." ;
