concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-20d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20D Dealing with unsolicited credit information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20d ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a credit reporting body receives credit information about an individual; and  (b) the body did not solicit the information; the body must, within a reasonable period after receiving the information, determine whether or not the body could have collected the information under section 20C if the body had solicited the information.  (2) The credit reporting body may use or disclose the credit information for the purposes of making the determination under subsection (1).  (3) If the credit reporting body determines that it could have collected the credit information, sections 20E to 20ZA apply in relation to" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a credit reporting body receives credit information about an individual; and  (b) the body did not solicit the information; the body must, within a reasonable period after receiving the information, determine whether or not the body could have collected the information under section 20C if the body had solicited the information.  (2) The credit reporting body may use or disclose the credit information for the purposes of making the determination under subsection (1).  (3) If the credit reporting body determines that it could have collected the credit information, sections 20E to 20ZA apply in relation to"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "211c5b4fbe648946e9a191672f4ba81c68b3759449af5b5963927cfe38c91592" ;
    cof:pageNumber "121"^^xsd:integer ;
