concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-20e-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20E(4) Use or disclosure of credit reporting information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20e-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) However, if the credit reporting information is, or was derived from, repayment history information or financial hardship information about the individual, the credit reporting body must not disclose the information under paragraph (3)(a) or (f) unless the recipient of the information is:  (a) a credit provider who is a licensee or is prescribed by the regulations; or  (b) a mortgage insurer. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "(4) However, if the credit reporting information is, or was derived from, repayment history information or financial hardship information about the individual, the credit reporting body must not disclose the information under paragraph (3)(a) or (f) unless the recipient of the information is:  (a) a credit provider who is a licensee or is prescribed by the regulations; or  (b) a mortgage insurer. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4f599d34e12ad61893dbd0cd981ab528aa4ee27d6ab225f732d520d857b39607" ;
    values:partOf concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-20e ;
    cof:pageNumber "122"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Do not disclose credit reporting information about financial hardship unless recipient is a licensed credit provider or mortgage insurer." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <entries-found-privacy-act-1988.pdf> ;
    dc:source "entries-found-privacy-act-1988.pdf, p.122" ;
