concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-20j a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20J Destruction of pre-screening assessment"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-20j ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an entity has possession or control of a pre-screening assessment, the entity must destroy the assessment if:  (a) the entity no longer needs the assessment for any purpose for which it may be used or disclosed under section 20H; and  (b) the entity is not required by or under an Australian law, or a court/tribunal order, to retain the assessment. Civil penalty: 1,000 penalty units.  (2) If the entity is an APP entity but not a credit reporting body, Australian Privacy Principle 11.2 does not apply to the entity in relation to the pre-screening assessment." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an entity has possession or control of a pre-screening assessment, the entity must destroy the assessment if:  (a) the entity no longer needs the assessment for any purpose for which it may be used or disclosed under section 20H; and  (b) the entity is not required by or under an Australian law, or a court/tribunal order, to retain the assessment. Civil penalty: 1,000 penalty units.  (2) If the entity is an APP entity but not a credit reporting body, Australian Privacy Principle 11.2 does not apply to the entity in relation to the pre-screening assessment."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c852ae7e23ab557d8bc3ec182f324882dd28a67417049492071b8f4f9951bd4e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "129"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-20j-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-20j-ss-2 ;
