    skos:definition "(1) If an entity has possession or control of a pre-screening assessment, the entity must destroy the assessment if:  (a) the entity no longer needs the assessment for any purpose for which it may be used or disclosed under section 20H; and  (b) the entity is not required by or under an Australian law, or a court/tribunal order, to retain the assessment. Civil penalty: 1,000 penalty units."@en ;
