doc:sch-2-sec-20j-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20J(1) Destruction of pre-screening assessment" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an entity has possession or control of a pre-screening assessment, the entity must destroy the assessment if:  (a) the entity no longer needs the assessment for any purpose for which it may be used or disclosed under section 20H; and  (b) the entity is not required by or under an Australian law, or a court/tribunal order, to retain the assessment. Civil penalty: 1,000 penalty units." ;
