concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-21g-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21G(2) Use or disclosure of credit eligibility information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21g-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the use of credit eligibility information about the individual if:  (a) the use is for a consumer credit related purpose of the credit provider in relation to the individual; or  (b) the use is a permitted CP use in relation to the individual; or  (c) both of the following apply:  (i) the credit provider believes on reasonable grounds that the individual has committed a serious credit infringement;  (ii) the provider uses the information in connection with the infringement; or  (d) the use is required or authorised by or under an Australian law (other than the consumer data rules) or a court/tribunal order; or  (e) the use is a use prescribed by the regulations. Permitted disclosures" ;
    skos:definition "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the use of credit eligibility information about the individual if:  (a) the use is for a consumer credit related purpose of the credit provider in relation to the individual; or  (b) the use is a permitted CP use in relation to the individual; or  (c) both of the following apply:  (i) the credit provider believes on reasonable grounds that the individual has committed a serious credit infringement;  (ii) the provider uses the information in connection with the infringement; or  (d) the use is required or authorised by or under an Australian law (other than the consumer data rules) or a court/tribunal order; or  (e) the use is a use prescribed by the regulations. Permitted disclosures"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1a811a0e5c90dd7e06b75c9f7dd94218575c56a3d160584e3c5213cd5cde9e99" ;
