concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-21q a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21Q Quality of credit eligibility information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21q ;
    values:originalText "(1) A credit provider must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in the circumstances to ensure that the credit eligibility information the provider collects is accurate, up-to-date and complete.  (2) A credit provider must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in the circumstances to ensure that the credit eligibility information the provider uses or discloses is, having regard to the purpose of the use or disclosure, accurate, up-to-date, complete and relevant.  (3) If a credit provider is an APP entity, Australian Privacy Principle 10 does not apply to the provider in relation to credit eligibility information." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A credit provider must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in the circumstances to ensure that the credit eligibility information the provider collects is accurate, up-to-date and complete.  (2) A credit provider must take such steps (if any) as are reasonable in the circumstances to ensure that the credit eligibility information the provider uses or discloses is, having regard to the purpose of the use or disclosure, accurate, up-to-date, complete and relevant.  (3) If a credit provider is an APP entity, Australian Privacy Principle 10 does not apply to the provider in relation to credit eligibility information."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2f92d52d640fc5102028b2cffc2e8e7f68ab8af56caab13db520867967fd5768" ;
    cof:pageNumber "169"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-21q-ss-1 ;
