concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-21w-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21W(2) Notice of correction etc. must be given"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-21w-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the credit provider corrects personal information about the individual under subsection 21V(2), the provider must, within a reasonable period:  (a) give the individual written notice of the correction; and  (b) if the provider consulted an interested party under subsection 21V(3) about the individual’s request—give the party written notice of the correction; and  (c) if the correction relates to information that the provider has previously disclosed under:  (i) this Division (other than subsection 21V(4)); or  (ii) the Australian Privacy Principles (other than Australian Privacy Principle 4.2);  give each recipient of the information written notice of the correction." ;
