    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-2-sec-23a-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "23A(2) Individual may complain about a breach of a provision of this" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) An individual may complain to a credit provider about an act or practice engaged in by the provider that may be a breach of either of the following provisions in relation to the individual:  (a) a provision of this Part (other than section 21T or 21V);  (b) a provision of the registered CR code (other than a provision that relates to that section) if it binds the credit provider.   Credit reporting  Part IIIA Complaints  Division 5  Section 23B  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Note: A complaint about a breach of section 21T or 21V, or a provision of the registered CR code that relates to that section, may be made to the Commissioner under Part V. Nature of complaint" ;
    cof:pageNumber "186"^^xsd:integer .

