concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-24a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24A Obtaining credit eligibility information from a credit provider"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-24a ;
    values:originalText "Offences  (1) An entity commits an offence if:  (a) the entity obtains credit eligibility information; and  (b) the information is obtained from a credit provider; and  (c) the entity is not:  (i) an entity to which the provider is permitted to disclose the information under Division 3 of this Part; or  (ii) an access seeker for the information. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  (2) An entity commits an offence if:  (a) the entity obtains credit eligibility information; and  (b) the information is obtained from a credit provider; and  (c) the information is obtained by false pretence. Penalty: 200 penalty units. Civil penalties  (3) An entity must not obtain credit eligibility information from a credit provider if the entity is not:  (a) an entity to which the provider is permitted to disclose the information under Division 3 of this Part; or  (b) an access seeker for the information. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units.   Credit reporting  Part IIIA Unauthorised obtaining of credit reporting information etc.  Division 6  Section 24A  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (4) An entity must not obtain, by false pretence, credit eligibility information from a credit provider. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "Offences  (1) An entity commits an offence if:  (a) the entity obtains credit eligibility information; and  (b) the information is obtained from a credit provider; and  (c) the entity is not:  (i) an entity to which the provider is permitted to disclose the information under Division 3 of this Part; or  (ii) an access seeker for the information. Penalty: 200 penalty units.  (2) An entity commits an offence if:  (a) the entity obtains credit eligibility information; and  (b) the information is obtained from a credit provider; and  (c) the information is obtained by false pretence. Penalty: 200 penalty units. Civil penalties  (3) An entity must not obtain credit eligibility information from a credit provider if the entity is not:  (a) an entity to which the provider is permitted to disclose the information under Division 3 of this Part; or  (b) an access seeker for the information. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units.   Credit reporting  Part IIIA Unauthorised obtaining of credit reporting information etc.  Division 6  Section 24A  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (4) An entity must not obtain, by false pretence, credit eligibility information from a credit provider. Civil penalty: 2,000 penalty units."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "87d390231948a0c49033f78db1046b1c0ea049452008ec1792ea0a263799dcc6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "192"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-24a-ss-1 ;
