concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-26c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26C What is an APP code"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-26c ;
    values:originalText "(1) An APP code is a written code of practice about information privacy.  (2) An APP code must:  (a) set out how one or more of the Australian Privacy Principles are to be applied or complied with; and  (b) specify the APP entities that are bound by the code, or a way of determining the APP entities that are bound by the code; and  (c) set out the period during which the code is in force (which must not start before the day the code is registered under section 26H)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An APP code is a written code of practice about information privacy.  (2) An APP code must:  (a) set out how one or more of the Australian Privacy Principles are to be applied or complied with; and  (b) specify the APP entities that are bound by the code, or a way of determining the APP entities that are bound by the code; and  (c) set out the period during which the code is in force (which must not start before the day the code is registered under section 26H)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4230c2617bdc0c77e77ce0366e9f974554836bed72c58297a5109cae2288dbc2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "199"^^xsd:integer ;
