concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-26ga a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26GA Development of APP codes by the Commissioner—at the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-26ga ;
    values:originalText "direction of the Minister Minister may give direction  (1) The Minister may, in writing, direct the Commissioner to develop an APP code if the Minister is satisfied that it is in the public interest:  (a) to develop the code; and  (b) for the Commissioner to develop the code.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a direction under that subsection may:  (a) specify one or more matters that the code must deal with; and  (b) specify the APP entities, or a class of APP entities, that are to be bound by the code.  (3) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument. Commissioner must develop and register code  (4) The Commissioner must develop and register an APP code if the Minister has given the Commissioner a direction under subsection (1) to develop the code." ;
    skos:definition "direction of the Minister Minister may give direction  (1) The Minister may, in writing, direct the Commissioner to develop an APP code if the Minister is satisfied that it is in the public interest:  (a) to develop the code; and  (b) for the Commissioner to develop the code.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a direction under that subsection may:  (a) specify one or more matters that the code must deal with; and  (b) specify the APP entities, or a class of APP entities, that are to be bound by the code.  (3) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument. Commissioner must develop and register code  (4) The Commissioner must develop and register an APP code if the Minister has given the Commissioner a direction under subsection (1) to develop the code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "09a0b236533a2332b3853f41994488c993c96868ec9aaa3cfce3e85410a57e03" ;
