    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If:  (a) an unauthorised access to information; or  (b) an unauthorised disclosure of information; or  (c) a loss of information; has been, or is required to be, notified under section 75 of the My Health Records Act 2012, this Part does not apply in relation to the access, disclosure or loss.   Notification of eligible data breaches  Part IIIC Eligible data breach  Division 2  Section 26WE  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer .

concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-26we a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26WE Eligible data breach"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-26we ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) both:  (i) an APP entity holds personal information relating to one or more individuals; and  (ii) the APP entity is required under section 15 not to do an act, or engage in a practice, that breaches Australian Privacy Principle 11.1 in relation to the personal information; or  (b) both:  (i) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information relating to one or more individuals; and  (ii) the credit reporting body is required to comply with section 20Q in relation to the credit reporting information; or  (c) both:  (i) a credit provider holds credit eligibility information relating to one or more individuals; and  (ii) the credit provider is required to comply with subsection 21S(1) in relation to the credit eligibility information; or  (d) both:  (i) a file number recipient holds tax file number information relating to one or more individuals; and  (ii) the file number recipient is required under section 18 not to do an act, or engage in a practice, that breaches a section 17 rule that relates to the tax file number information." ;
    skos:definition "Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) both:  (i) an APP entity holds personal information relating to one or more individuals; and  (ii) the APP entity is required under section 15 not to do an act, or engage in a practice, that breaches Australian Privacy Principle 11.1 in relation to the personal information; or  (b) both:  (i) a credit reporting body holds credit reporting information relating to one or more individuals; and  (ii) the credit reporting body is required to comply with section 20Q in relation to the credit reporting information; or  (c) both:  (i) a credit provider holds credit eligibility information relating to one or more individuals; and  (ii) the credit provider is required to comply with subsection 21S(1) in relation to the credit eligibility information; or  (d) both:  (i) a file number recipient holds tax file number information relating to one or more individuals; and  (ii) the file number recipient is required under section 18 not to do an act, or engage in a practice, that breaches a section 17 rule that relates to the tax file number information."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "94d86fb5736a350839bbef0a9304ec30d34f3cc2c1bb256e999d7cd85b566b35" ;
    cof:pageNumber "223"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "An APP entity must comply with section 15 if it holds personal information relating to one or more individuals." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <entries-found-privacy-act-1988.pdf> ;
    dc:source "entries-found-privacy-act-1988.pdf, p.223" ;
    cml:asserts concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-26we-norm .
concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-26we-norm a values:Obligation ;
