concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-49b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "49B Transfer of complaints from the Inspector-General of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-49b ;
    values:originalText "Intelligence and Security  An individual is taken to have complained to the Information Commissioner under subsection 36(1) in respect of action taken by ACC, the Australian Federal Police, AUSTRAC or the Department of Home Affairs (within the meaning of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986) if the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security transfers all or part of the complaint to the Information Commissioner under section 32AG of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986." ;
    skos:definition "Intelligence and Security  An individual is taken to have complained to the Information Commissioner under subsection 36(1) in respect of action taken by ACC, the Australian Federal Police, AUSTRAC or the Department of Home Affairs (within the meaning of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986) if the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security transfers all or part of the complaint to the Information Commissioner under section 32AG of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9f98c468cf84af3f1a83d9b45c59e644b10e64a42fd829959427b531b72531d4" ;
