    values:originalText "(7) In this section: designated secrecy provision means any of the following:  (a) sections 18, 18A, 18B, 34GF, 35P, 92 and 92A, and subsection 34GE(4), of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979;  (aa) section 15LC of the Crimes Act 1914;  (b) section 34 of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986;  (c) sections 39, 40C, 40D and 41 of, and clause 9 of Schedule 1 to, the Intelligence Services Act 2001;  (ca) sections 42 to 44 of the Office of National Intelligence Act 2018;  (cb) sections 22, 22A and 22B of the Witness Protection Act 1994;  (d) a provision of a Commonwealth law prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph;  (e) a provision of a Commonwealth law of a kind prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this paragraph." ;
