concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-80tc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "80TC Modifications of Part 2 of the Regulatory Powers Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-80tc ;
    values:originalText "Use of force in executing a monitoring warrant  In executing a monitoring warrant under Part 2 of the Regulatory Powers Act, as that Part applies in relation to the provisions mentioned in subsection 80TB(1), the information mentioned in subsection 80TB(2), and the matters mentioned in subsection 80TB(3), of this Act:  (a) an authorised person may use such force against things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  (b) a person assisting the authorised person may use such force against things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances.   Compliance and enforcement  Part VIB Investigation powers  Division 1AC  Section 80TD  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Division 1AC—Investigation powers" ;
    skos:definition "Use of force in executing a monitoring warrant  In executing a monitoring warrant under Part 2 of the Regulatory Powers Act, as that Part applies in relation to the provisions mentioned in subsection 80TB(1), the information mentioned in subsection 80TB(2), and the matters mentioned in subsection 80TB(3), of this Act:  (a) an authorised person may use such force against things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  (b) a person assisting the authorised person may use such force against things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances.   Compliance and enforcement  Part VIB Investigation powers  Division 1AC  Section 80TD  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Division 1AC—Investigation powers"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "034f99fa61666ed4338807ac8a854c8f09232b7ebb7967bd7f9640df050bec5b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "344"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Use of force in executing a monitoring warrant" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
