concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-2-sec-89 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "89 Obligations of confidence to which Part applies"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-89 ;
    values:originalText "Unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in this Part to an obligation of confidence is a reference to an obligation of confidence:  (a) to which an agency or a Commonwealth officer is subject, however the obligation arose; or  (b) that arises under or by virtue of the law in force in the Australian Capital Territory; or  (c) that arises under or by virtue of a law in force in an external Territory." ;
    skos:definition "Unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in this Part to an obligation of confidence is a reference to an obligation of confidence:  (a) to which an agency or a Commonwealth officer is subject, however the obligation arose; or  (b) that arises under or by virtue of the law in force in the Australian Capital Territory; or  (c) that arises under or by virtue of a law in force in an external Territory."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b617b0b1e6d369b61a2d822d39851b98941e684cd6ed5366ceb3714fa798a1a1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "364"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Reference to an obligation of confidence in this Part." ;
