doc:sch-1-sec-7-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "7 1 If an organisation holds personal information about an individual," ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "the organisation must not use or disclose the information for the purpose of direct marketing. Note: An act or practice of an agency may be treated as an act or practice of an organisation, see section 7A. Exceptions—personal information other than sensitive information" ;
    cof:pageNumber "389"^^xsd:integer .

concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-1-sec-7-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "7 2 Despite subclause 7.1, an organisation may use or disclose"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-7-3 ;
    values:originalText "personal information (other than sensitive information) about an individual for the purpose of direct marketing if:  (a) the organisation collected the information from the individual; and  (b) the individual would reasonably expect the organisation to use or disclose the information for that purpose; and  (c) the organisation provides a simple means by which the individual may easily request not to receive direct marketing communications from the organisation; and  Schedule 1  Australian Privacy Principles" ;
    skos:definition "personal information (other than sensitive information) about an individual for the purpose of direct marketing if:  (a) the organisation collected the information from the individual; and  (b) the individual would reasonably expect the organisation to use or disclose the information for that purpose; and  (c) the organisation provides a simple means by which the individual may easily request not to receive direct marketing communications from the organisation; and  Schedule 1  Australian Privacy Principles"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "daa6101c563f7e4ea1e4407dcbd438b9b622d54ad531397051d00d619d464968" ;
