doc:sch-1-sec-12-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "12 1 If an APP entity holds personal information about an individual," ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "the entity must, on request by the individual, give the individual access to the information. Exception to access—agency" ;
    cof:pageNumber "398"^^xsd:integer .

concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-1-sec-12-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12 2 If:"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-12-3 ;
    values:originalText "(a) the APP entity is an agency; and  (b) the entity is required or authorised to refuse to give the individual access to the personal information by or under:  (i) the Freedom of Information Act; or  (ii) any other Act of the Commonwealth, or a law in force in an external Territory, that provides for access by persons to documents; then, despite subclause 12.1, the entity is not required to give access to the extent that the entity is required or authorised to refuse to give access. Exception to access—organisation" ;
    skos:definition "(a) the APP entity is an agency; and  (b) the entity is required or authorised to refuse to give the individual access to the personal information by or under:  (i) the Freedom of Information Act; or  (ii) any other Act of the Commonwealth, or a law in force in an external Territory, that provides for access by persons to documents; then, despite subclause 12.1, the entity is not required to give access to the extent that the entity is required or authorised to refuse to give access. Exception to access—organisation"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a658733f396b4027778179663f3b5d8de261bd03098e6d72de0264d5e11c5e8d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "398"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Entity may refuse access to personal information under certain Acts or laws." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <entries-found-privacy-act-1988.pdf> ;
    dc:source "entries-found-privacy-act-1988.pdf, p.398" ;
    cml:asserts concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-1-sec-12-3-norm .
concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-1-sec-12-3-norm a values:Prohibition ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    values:partOf concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-1-sec-12-3 ;
    values:borneBy values:State ;
    skos:scopeNote "borne by: State" ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-1-sec-12-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "12 2 If:" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(a) the APP entity is an agency; and  (b) the entity is required or authorised to refuse to give the individual access to the personal information by or under:  (i) the Freedom of Information Act; or  (ii) any other Act of the Commonwealth, or a law in force in an external Territory, that provides for access by persons to documents; then, despite subclause 12.1, the entity is not required to give access to the extent that the entity is required or authorised to refuse to give access. Exception to access—organisation" ;
    cof:pageNumber "398"^^xsd:integer .

concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-1-sec-12-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12 3 If the APP entity is an organisation then, despite subclause 12.1,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-12-4 ;
    values:originalText "the entity is not required to give the individual access to the personal information to the extent that:  (a) the entity reasonably believes that giving access would pose a serious threat to the life, health or safety of any individual, or to public health or public safety; or  (b) giving access would have an unreasonable impact on the privacy of other individuals; or  Australian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1 Access to, and correction of, personal information  Part 5  Clause 12  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) the request for access is frivolous or vexatious; or  (d) the information relates to existing or anticipated legal proceedings between the entity and the individual, and would not be accessible by the process of discovery in those proceedings; or  (e) giving access would reveal the intentions of the entity in relation to negotiations with the individual in such a way as to prejudice those negotiations; or  (f) giving access would be unlawful; or  (g) denying access is required or authorised by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; or  (h) both of the following apply:  (i) the entity has reason to suspect that unlawful activity, or misconduct of a serious nature, that relates to the entity’s functions or activities has been, is being or may be engaged in;  (ii) giving access would be likely to prejudice the taking of appropriate action in relation to the matter; or  (i) giving access would be likely to prejudice one or more enforcement related activities conducted by, or on behalf of, an enforcement body; or  (j) giving access would reveal evaluative information generated within the entity in connection with a commercially sensitive decision-making process. Dealing with requests for access" ;
    skos:definition "the entity is not required to give the individual access to the personal information to the extent that:  (a) the entity reasonably believes that giving access would pose a serious threat to the life, health or safety of any individual, or to public health or public safety; or  (b) giving access would have an unreasonable impact on the privacy of other individuals; or  Australian Privacy Principles  Schedule 1 Access to, and correction of, personal information  Part 5  Clause 12  Privacy Act 1988  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) the request for access is frivolous or vexatious; or  (d) the information relates to existing or anticipated legal proceedings between the entity and the individual, and would not be accessible by the process of discovery in those proceedings; or  (e) giving access would reveal the intentions of the entity in relation to negotiations with the individual in such a way as to prejudice those negotiations; or  (f) giving access would be unlawful; or  (g) denying access is required or authorised by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; or  (h) both of the following apply:  (i) the entity has reason to suspect that unlawful activity, or misconduct of a serious nature, that relates to the entity’s functions or activities has been, is being or may be engaged in;  (ii) giving access would be likely to prejudice the taking of appropriate action in relation to the matter; or  (i) giving access would be likely to prejudice one or more enforcement related activities conducted by, or on behalf of, an enforcement body; or  (j) giving access would reveal evaluative information generated within the entity in connection with a commercially sensitive decision-making process. Dealing with requests for access"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cf92ffb07d2a5f59757984fc07a7064958da3a949b65a402d6c1184a3ceae43c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "398"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Entity not required to give individual access to personal information under certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <entries-found-privacy-act-1988.pdf> ;
    dc:source "entries-found-privacy-act-1988.pdf, p.398" ;
    cml:asserts concept:entries-found-privacy-act-1988-sch-1-sec-12-4-norm .
